  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "In a medium microwave safe bowl, mix cucumber, salt, onion, mustard seeds, white sugar, distilled white vinegar, celery seed and turmeric.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Microwave on high 7 to 8 minutes, stirring twice, until cucumbers are tender and onion is translucent.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Transfer to sterile containers. Seal and chill in the refrigerator until serving.",
      "group": null
    }
  ],
  "footnotes": [],
  "nutrition": null,
  "importedNotes": [
    {
      "text": "So easy, so quick, so good! Better make a double batch cause they don't last long. You can eat them as soon as they get cold!"
    },
    {
      "text": "I did make one variation: I added dehydrated red cayenne peppers for color and a bit of spice."
    }
